#: ../../../developer_guide/cpp_style.md:1
msgid "C++ Style Guide"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer_guide/cpp_style.md:3
msgid ""
"TileLang C++ code should be easy to read for contributors who already know "
"TVM. Use TVM's C++ conventions as the baseline, with small TileLang-specific "
"rules where the compiler, runtime, or generated kernel templates need them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer_guide/cpp_style.md:7
msgid ""
"This guide applies to C++ source under `src/` and TileLang-owned headers. Do "
"not apply broad style-only churn to vendored code under `3rdparty/` or "
"generated runtime templates unless a local change already needs to touch "
"that code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer_guide/cpp_style.md:11
msgid "Formatting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer_guide/cpp_style.md:13
msgid "Run the repository formatter before sending a pull request:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer_guide/cpp_style.md:15
msgid "bash format.sh --files <changed-file>...\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer_guide/cpp_style.md:19
msgid "For all changed files relative to the merge base:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer_guide/cpp_style.md:21
msgid "bash format.sh\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer_guide/cpp_style.md:25
msgid ""
"Formatting is mechanical. Keep style changes separate from behavior changes "
"when the diff would otherwise become noisy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer_guide/cpp_style.md:28
msgid ""
"TileLang aims to stay close to TVM's Google-based C++ formatting. If the "
"repository `.clang-format` is changed, do it in a focused pull request and "
"avoid mixing that change with semantic edits."
msgstr ""

